   "researcher_notes": "Runs generally north-to-south down the Baghdad governorate: from Taji (~25-30 km north of central Baghdad) to the Al-Dora/Daura district on the south side of the city (Dora oil refinery and Al-Dora thermal/gas power stations). Straight-line ~28 km; a routed alignment skirting/through the metro is plausibly ~45-55 km, consistent with the likely-duplicate P1845 'Taji-South Baghdad' length of 56 km. Endpoints are named at town/facility scale and independently verifiable; the intermediate alignment is NOT sourced -- treat as a loose Baghdad-governorate corridor, not a traced route. Endpoints established from the pipeline NAME (Taji -> Duara/Dora) plus the Jafar/Uruk map placing the line on the north-south Baghdad dry-gas backbone. The two proposed_refs are verifier-passing and confirm the ENDPOINTS exist as real Baghdad-area places (Taji town north of Baghdad; Al-Dora power station in Dora, south Baghdad) -- they do NOT independently confirm the pipeline between them. Coordinates are approximate, decimal-degree EPSG:4326, defensible from these named, well-known places (Taji town center ~33.52N 44.23E; Dora refinery/power complex, south Baghdad ~33.27N 44.40E); no coordinate was fabricated and the intermediate waypoint is an approximate metro transit point, not a sourced vertex. If the row is merged into P1845 per the duplicate finding, transfer this corridor there."
